1
00:00:04,386 --> 00:00:06,899
The Lives of the Prophets Part 2;

2
00:00:27,218 --> 00:00:31,090
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

3
00:00:32,078 --> 00:00:37,453
The next story; is the longest story of a Nabi(نَبِي) in Qur'an.

4
00:00:40,718 --> 00:00:47,655
It is the story of Al-Kaleem(ألكليم) Musa عليه الصلواة والسّلام.

5
00:00:48,468 --> 00:01:00,139
Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى) was mentioned in more than 30 positions or Su'ar(سورة) in Qur'an and he was mentioned 124 times.

6
00:01:02,159 --> 00:01:03,692
One of the scholars said;

7
00:01:03,786 --> 00:01:06,811
كاد القران ان يكون موسى

8
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:11,204
Qur'an was almost going to become the story of Musa(موسى).

9
00:01:13,291 --> 00:01:18,295
The story of Musa(موسى) was mentioned so many times in Qur'an that this scholar said;

10
00:01:18,555 --> 00:01:25,473
Qur'an was almost going to be the story of Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى); A Hundred and 24 times

11
00:01:27,587 --> 00:01:31,711
There's no other Nabi(نَبِي) in Qur'an; who's mentioned more than Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى).

12
00:01:32,365 --> 00:01:41,679
And there is no story that takes a longer space and span of Qur'an discussed in elaborate details, in many positions of Qur'an, like the story of Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى).

13
00:01:42,392 --> 00:01:43,252
Why?

14
00:01:43,979 --> 00:01:49,785
Is it because he's one of the greatest Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء); he's one of Uulul Azam(أولو العزم); the five strongest prophets;

15
00:01:49,839 --> 00:01:54,991
which are Muhammadﷺ, Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم), Musa(موسى), Eesa(عيسى) and Nuh(نوح), these are the five.

16
00:01:55,291 --> 00:01:56,824
Is it because of that?

17
00:01:57,284 --> 00:01:59,916
Well, Ibrahim عليه السّلام is also one of Uulul Azam(أولو العزم);

18
00:01:59,969 --> 00:02:06,935
Infact Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) says that the opinion of the scholars is; that the best Nabi(نَبِي) after Muhammadﷺ is Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم)

19
00:02:08,562 --> 00:02:15,736
but the story of Ibrahim عليه السّلام is not mentioned as frequently, it comes nowhere close to the details of the story of Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى).

20
00:02:16,016 --> 00:02:20,505
So how come this story was mentioned in so much details in Qur'an?

21
00:02:20,951 --> 00:02:23,292
There's a few reasonsl; Let's go through them.

22
00:02:23,512 --> 00:02:35,307
Number one; The Ummah(امة) of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) are the last Muslim Ummah(امة), before the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ.

23
00:02:37,627 --> 00:02:40,254
You know that there are many Muslim nations throughout history.

24
00:02:41,447 --> 00:02:47,735
The Ummah(امة) of Nuh(نوح), the Ummah(امة)  of Adam(آدَم), the Ummah(امة) of Hud(هود), the Ummah(امة) of Saleh(صالح)

25
00:02:48,402 --> 00:02:52,131
the last Ummah(امة) is the Ummah(امة) of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

26
00:02:53,752 --> 00:02:57,805
So they are the closest in proximity to the Ummah(امة)  of Muhammadﷺ.

27
00:02:58,358 --> 00:03:06,157
And since this Ummah(امة) of  Muhammadﷺ, are the inheritors of all of the former and previous messages;

28
00:03:06,457 --> 00:03:11,970
it is important for us to know the Ummah(امة) that was right before us; the ones who are proceeding us.

29
00:03:12,223 --> 00:03:13,043
Number two;

30
00:03:13,377 --> 00:03:21,095
The history of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) is extremely rich with experiences.

31
00:03:22,338 --> 00:03:28,052
It is an Ummah(امة) that lived for a long time lasted for a while, they went through a lot.

32
00:03:28,852 --> 00:03:30,784
They committed a lot of mistakes.

33
00:03:31,291 --> 00:03:36,509
There was a lot of misguidance there was a lot of conflicts.

34
00:03:36,749 --> 00:03:42,443
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wanted us to have all of this experience in front of our eyes;

35
00:03:42,796 --> 00:03:49,956
so that we could use it in our, Da'wah(دعوة) in our long history as the Muslim Ummah(امة).

36
00:03:50,343 --> 00:03:53,978
The Ummah(امة) of Musa(موسى) went through experiences;

37
00:03:54,008 --> 00:03:59,026
Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل), they went through experiences and they committed mistakes.

38
00:03:59,618 --> 00:04:06,993
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى knew that Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ would fall in the same particular mistakes that Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) fell into,

39
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:11,093
and that's why it's important for us to have a history to look back to.

40
00:04:12,413 --> 00:04:13,671
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

41
00:04:13,701 --> 00:04:16,004
لتتبعن سنن من كان قبلكم،

42
00:04:16,267 --> 00:04:20,253
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; You would follow the footsteps of the nations before you;

43
00:04:20,520 --> 00:04:29,486
Step by step, inch by inch, foot by foot, even if they are going to enter into a hole of a lizard, you would follow them and do it.

44
00:04:30,066 --> 00:04:32,246
The Sahabah(صحابه) said; Are you talking about the Jews and Christians.?

45
00:04:32,306 --> 00:04:33,365
Rasool Ullah said; Who else.

46
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:36,915
We are going to follow the tracks.

47
00:04:37,501 --> 00:04:40,421
We're going to follow their tracks, we're going to do the same thing as they did.

48
00:04:40,568 --> 00:04:42,195
We're going to commit the same mistakes.

49
00:04:42,825 --> 00:04:53,373
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given us this wealth of information and experience so that it could be light for us; the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ.

50
00:04:54,197 --> 00:04:55,277
Number three;

51
00:04:55,750 --> 00:05:03,508
The nature of the conflict of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) is similar to the nature of the conflict of the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ.

52
00:05:03,951 --> 00:05:06,114
With the people of Hud(هود); How were they destroyed?

53
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:07,781
Violent wind.

54
00:05:08,294 --> 00:05:10,228
The people of Saleh(صالح); How were they destroyed?

55
00:05:11,298 --> 00:05:12,358
By the Sieha(صيحا).

56
00:05:12,792 --> 00:05:14,771
The people of Lut(لوط); How were they destroyed?

57
00:05:15,184 --> 00:05:19,064
By the shaking of the earth and lifting them up and throwing them down.

58
00:05:19,363 --> 00:05:24,603
So did, Hud عليه السّلام and his followers fight in Jihad(جهاد) against their people?

59
00:05:24,990 --> 00:05:25,470
No.

60
00:05:25,730 --> 00:05:29,015
Did Saleh(صالح) fight in Jihad(جهاد) against his people actual war?

61
00:05:29,129 --> 00:05:29,822
No.

62
00:05:30,609 --> 00:05:32,142
What about with Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل)?

63
00:05:32,835 --> 00:05:34,515
Did they fight against their enemies?

64
00:05:34,882 --> 00:05:35,689
Yes.

65
00:05:36,791 --> 00:05:41,432
And that's why; one of the scholar said; Since the Torah(توراة) was revealed, it was Jihad(جهاد).

66
00:05:42,466 --> 00:05:49,774
It wasn't special punishments coming from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى but it was punishing the enemy through the hands of the believers

67
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:53,494
instead of Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل), destroying them or a violent wind.

68
00:05:53,834 --> 00:06:00,494
Now since the Torah(توراة) was revealed; It is Allahسُبحانه وتعالى destroying the enemy with the hands of the believers.

69
00:06:01,513 --> 00:06:03,259
And that is Al-Qital Fee Sabil Lillah(القتال فى سبيل الله)

70
00:06:03,366 --> 00:06:06,406
and that is why the nature of the conflict between

71
00:06:06,619 --> 00:06:12,421
the Ummah(امة) of Musa(موسى) and their enemies is similar to the nature of the conflict between the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ and his enemies.

72
00:06:12,647 --> 00:06:18,307
With the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ, we didn't have a violent wind destroying them or earthquake

73
00:06:18,501 --> 00:06:25,777
even though sometimes Allah would send these miracles but overall, it is through the hands of the believers, the enemy is destroyed.

74
00:06:26,350 --> 00:06:29,902
So there is a similarity in the nature of the conflict.

75
00:06:30,509 --> 00:06:31,769
Number four;

76
00:06:32,095 --> 00:06:33,987
There are two halves of the story of Musa(موسى);

77
00:06:34,182 --> 00:06:36,996
one half is Musa(موسى) and Firaon(فرعون)

78
00:06:37,530 --> 00:06:39,956
and the other half is Musa(موسى) and Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

79
00:06:40,730 --> 00:06:46,296
There are two parts; Both of these are very, very important for us to know.

80
00:06:47,242 --> 00:06:53,927
The part of the conflict between Musa(موسى) and Firaon(فرعون) is very, very important to us

81
00:06:53,957 --> 00:06:58,661
because Firaon(فرعون) is the symbol of tyranny, dictatorship and oppression.

82
00:06:59,657 --> 00:07:04,821
And Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله) we find that, that is the problem that the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ is suffering through.

83
00:07:05,041 --> 00:07:09,917
We have suffered from oppression and tyranny and dictatorship for a very, very long time.

84
00:07:10,084 --> 00:07:14,277
And that's why it is very helpful for us to know the story of Firaon(فرعون).

85
00:07:15,708 --> 00:07:20,618
Because that is something that this Ummah(امة) has suffered from; for a long time; for centuries;

86
00:07:20,861 --> 00:07:25,351
we have suffered oppression and the symbol of oppression and Qur'an is Firaon(فرعون).

87
00:07:26,550 --> 00:07:29,298
So, how can we deal with that oppression?

88
00:07:29,518 --> 00:07:31,731
It is the way that Musa(موسى) have dealt with it.

89
00:07:32,151 --> 00:07:33,968
We learn a lot of experiences from that.

90
00:07:34,764 --> 00:07:39,369
And also Firaon(فرعون) is a king, power through kingdom.

91
00:07:39,941 --> 00:07:42,831
And that is, how Islam is being fought against.

92
00:07:43,097 --> 00:07:45,951
It is through the governments and powers of the throne.

93
00:07:46,371 --> 00:07:48,551
And Dajjal(دجال) is only an extension of that.

94
00:07:49,317 --> 00:07:52,847
Dajjal(دجال) is a king on a throne who will rule over the world.

95
00:07:53,667 --> 00:07:59,846
So that is why the story of Firaon(فرعون) would have a lot of similarities between it and the story of Al-Dajjal(الدجال) .

96
00:08:00,533 --> 00:08:04,466
And then we have the other half of the story of Musa(موسى) is;

97
00:08:04,526 --> 00:08:06,253
Musa(موسى) dealing with his people.

98
00:08:06,467 --> 00:08:10,213
How Musa(موسى) dealt with the Muslim Ummah(امة) of this time; Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).?

99
00:08:11,079 --> 00:08:15,059
When you see the faults and the problems of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل)

100
00:08:15,089 --> 00:08:18,266
even though they were the Ummah(امة) of Tawheed(تؤحيد), the Ummah(امة) of oneness of Allah.

101
00:08:19,172 --> 00:08:23,492
And you see the faults that we are falling into and getting into.

102
00:08:23,966 --> 00:08:27,479
You see how important it is to know the story of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

103
00:08:28,766 --> 00:08:32,486
In Qur'an su'ar Al-Maida(مائدة); there are Ayaat(آيات), where Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

104
00:08:32,516 --> 00:08:34,686
ومن لم يحكم بما أنزل الله فأولئك هم الكافرون۝

105
00:08:34,723 --> 00:08:35,846
فأولئك هم الفاسقون۝

106
00:08:35,876 --> 00:08:37,061
فأولئك هم الظالمون۝

107
00:08:37,301 --> 00:08:40,460
The ones who did not rule according to the book of Allah are the unbelievers;

108
00:08:40,753 --> 00:08:45,067
In other places, it says the corrupt and in other places says the oppressors.

109
00:08:45,558 --> 00:08:48,912
Hudhaifa-bin-Al-Yaman(حديفه بن اليمان) heard some of the tabaein(تابعين) speaking about this and they said;

110
00:08:49,066 --> 00:08:52,359
These Ayaat(آيات) were revealed speaking about Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

111
00:08:52,906 --> 00:08:58,294
He said; Allahu Akbar(الله اكبر), what better cousins to you are the children of Israel(اسرائيل).

112
00:08:58,445 --> 00:09:01,627
Whenever there is something bad in Qur'an; You say; it's speaking about them,

113
00:09:01,840 --> 00:09:04,946
and wherever there's something good in Quran; You say; it's speaking about you.

114
00:09:06,219 --> 00:09:12,544
He wants to teach them a lesson that these Ayaat(آيات) even though they are speaking about Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل),

115
00:09:12,710 --> 00:09:19,409
but whoever is similar to that; from this Ummah(امة) would receive the same punishment.

116
00:09:20,359 --> 00:09:22,249
That is why Allah mentioned it in Qur'an.

117
00:09:22,402 --> 00:09:24,344
If you do not rule over the book of Allah,

118
00:09:24,374 --> 00:09:27,899
whether you are from Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) or from any other nation,

119
00:09:28,272 --> 00:09:33,466
that is considered to be kufr(كفر) and it's considered to be dhulm(ظلم) and it's considered to be to fisq(فسق).

120
00:09:34,366 --> 00:09:38,604
Finally, the last reason that I have listed and there are many others.

121
00:09:39,316 --> 00:09:41,844
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has talked a lot about Al-Yahood(اليهود).

122
00:09:42,651 --> 00:09:49,392
Because it was in the knowledge of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, who knows everything (Al-Aleem العليم),

123
00:09:50,112 --> 00:09:59,863
that this band of people would be the enemies of the religion of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى from day one, until the Day of Judgment.

124
00:10:00,203 --> 00:10:05,389
Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله); the Jews are a very small nation and they have been a very small nation for a very long time.

125
00:10:05,419 --> 00:10:07,595
For centuries, the numbers of the Jews is very limited.

126
00:10:07,815 --> 00:10:12,244
Why didn't Allahسُبحانه وتعالى talk about the Hindus or the Buddhist or the Confucius,

127
00:10:12,463 --> 00:10:16,206
even though there are much more in numbers like He has talked about Al-Yahood(ال يهود)?

128
00:10:17,239 --> 00:10:19,126
Numbers is not the issue;

129
00:10:19,926 --> 00:10:28,625
Al-Yahood(اليهود) from day one, until this day, are the ones who are leading the war and the battle against Islam.

130
00:10:29,205 --> 00:10:33,745
They are the ones who are making the plans and the plots against this religion.

131
00:10:34,199 --> 00:10:40,019
The Yahood(يهود) are the ones, who supported the Munafiqeen(مُنافقين) in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ

132
00:10:40,243 --> 00:10:43,191
and they are the ones who are supporting the Munafiqeen(مُنافقين) today.

133
00:10:43,924 --> 00:10:52,451
Al-Yahood(اليهود) are the ones who planed together and brought the Ahzaab(احزاب); the Arab tribes together to fight against Rasool Allah ﷺ

134
00:10:52,644 --> 00:10:57,134
and the Jews are the ones who are bringing today the nations of the world against the Muslims.

135
00:10:58,326 --> 00:11:05,026
The Yahood(يهود) are the ones who we're taking care of the word propaganda against Islam.

136
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:10,256
And the Jews today are the ones, who are taking the lead in the media warfare against Islam.

137
00:11:11,402 --> 00:11:16,309
From day one, they have been the enemies of the religion of Muhammadﷺ,

138
00:11:16,462 --> 00:11:23,580
and they will continue to be the enemies until the last generation of Al-Yahood(اليهود) will be the soldiers and the supporters of the Al- Dajjal(الدجال).

139
00:11:23,927 --> 00:11:25,100
And then it will be the end.

140
00:11:26,740 --> 00:11:30,635
And that's why Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has talked about this nation so that we would know;

141
00:11:31,229 --> 00:11:32,536
وَاللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِأَعْدَائِكُمْ ۚ

142
00:11:32,566 --> 00:11:35,229
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; He is knows best who your enemies are.

143
00:11:35,948 --> 00:11:37,802
The story of Musa(موسى) is very long.

144
00:11:39,055 --> 00:11:45,730
It's a very detailed story, these Ayaat(آيات), or a summary of the story of Musa(موسى).

145
00:11:47,197 --> 00:11:48,754
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

146
00:11:49,225 --> 00:11:55,418
طسم ۝

147
00:11:55,618 --> 00:12:00,178
تِلْكَ آيَاتُ الْكِتَابِ الْمُبِينِ ۝

148
00:12:00,365 --> 00:12:08,723
نَتْلُو عَلَيْكَ مِن نَّبَإِ مُوسَىٰ وَفِرْعَوْنَ بِالْحَقِّ لِقَوْمٍ يُؤْمِنُونَ۝

149
00:12:09,256 --> 00:12:10,396
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says;

150
00:12:11,289 --> 00:12:15,569
We recite to you some of the news.

151
00:12:16,489 --> 00:12:17,653
This is News,

152
00:12:17,952 --> 00:12:27,273
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is conveying to you news, of Musa(موسى) and Firaon(فرعون).

153
00:12:27,933 --> 00:12:31,446
The difference between this news and other news that you hear;

154
00:12:31,619 --> 00:12:35,447
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says that, this news Bil-Haqq(حَقّ); in truth.

155
00:12:36,701 --> 00:12:39,654
Every other piece of news that you hear can be true and can be false.

156
00:12:39,954 --> 00:12:43,761
But this news Allahسُبحانه وتعالى tells you; Bil-Haqq(حَقّ), it is the true news.

157
00:12:44,614 --> 00:12:46,954
And, who is this directed to?

158
00:12:47,173 --> 00:12:48,461
 لِقَوْمٍ يُؤْمِنُونَ۝

159
00:12:48,528 --> 00:12:49,421
For the believers.

160
00:12:49,968 --> 00:12:56,678
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says, and this Ayah(آية) is describing the political and social situation in the time of Musa(موسى).

161
00:12:57,051 --> 00:12:59,471
ان فرعون على فلارض

162
00:13:00,255 --> 00:13:03,516
Firaon(فرعون) exalted himself in the land.

163
00:13:05,129 --> 00:13:07,500
This is the political situation in that time.

164
00:13:07,907 --> 00:13:12,659
Firaon(فرعون) was the only power figure.

165
00:13:13,726 --> 00:13:23,451
And he was so strong and powerful; and he had so much influence over the lives of people, that he thought that he is God.

166
00:13:24,504 --> 00:13:25,044
And he said;

167
00:13:25,074 --> 00:13:26,253
انا ربكم الاعلى

168
00:13:26,313 --> 00:13:27,493
I am your Lord.

169
00:13:27,906 --> 00:13:28,746
And then he said;

170
00:13:28,776 --> 00:13:30,636
وما علمتلكم من اله غيره

171
00:13:30,696 --> 00:13:33,191
I don't know that you have any other God but me.

172
00:13:33,451 --> 00:13:34,877
He has so much power;

173
00:13:34,907 --> 00:13:41,790
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given him so much power, that he could get away with this claim and nobody would protest it.

174
00:13:42,170 --> 00:13:44,848
When he said, I am your Lord and I am your God.

175
00:13:44,950 --> 00:13:46,204
Nobody said you're wrong.

176
00:13:46,857 --> 00:13:52,110
He got away with it, because he had so much influence and power over the lives of people.

177
00:13:52,777 --> 00:13:54,263
وجعل أهلها شيعا

178
00:13:54,323 --> 00:13:57,989
He divided the people into parties, and that is how you rule.

179
00:13:58,029 --> 00:13:58,783
Farriq Tasud(فرق تسد);

180
00:13:59,009 --> 00:14:00,143
Divide and Conquer.

181
00:14:01,422 --> 00:14:06,428
He divided the people in Egypt; into different classes, into different tribes.

182
00:14:06,728 --> 00:14:12,006
That is how you dominate by class conflict and by these conflicts in society;

183
00:14:12,126 --> 00:14:14,039
That is how the Kings rule.

184
00:14:14,966 --> 00:14:18,679
And Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) were placed on the lowest level; lowest class.

185
00:14:19,119 --> 00:14:22,988
And then he place these other groups from Egypt above them and over them.

186
00:14:23,208 --> 00:14:26,028
So Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) were taking as slaves and servants.

187
00:14:26,734 --> 00:14:29,139
يَسْتَضْعِفُ طَائِفَةً مِّنْهُمْ

188
00:14:29,512 --> 00:14:33,119
He oppressed a group of them which are the children of Israel(اسرائيل).

189
00:14:33,299 --> 00:14:40,055
 يُذَبِّحُ أَبْنَاءَهُمْ وَيَسْتَحْيِي نِسَاءَهُمْ ۚ

190
00:14:40,108 --> 00:14:42,615
The children of Israel(اسرائيل) have multiplied a lot.

191
00:14:43,382 --> 00:14:44,902
They started by who?

192
00:14:45,495 --> 00:14:46,802
By Yusuf(يوسف) and his brothers.

193
00:14:47,068 --> 00:14:49,222
But by now, they were already a huge nation;

194
00:14:49,308 --> 00:14:54,648
It says; they were about 600,000 at the time, when Musa(موسى) left with them out of Egypt.

195
00:14:54,982 --> 00:14:58,588
Anyway, Firaon(فرعون) saw a dream; it says that Firaon(فرعون) saw a dream.

196
00:14:59,202 --> 00:15:06,048
In this dream, It was interpreted that there's a child who will be born among the children of Israel(اسرائيل), who will take away your kingdom.

197
00:15:08,042 --> 00:15:11,531
When Firaon(فرعون) heard that interpretation, he said; it's easy, we'll take care of that.

198
00:15:12,638 --> 00:15:14,071
Any child who is born kill him.

199
00:15:14,898 --> 00:15:19,659
So he would kill all of the male children, and he would take the woman as slaves and servants.

200
00:15:20,466 --> 00:15:21,986
وَيَسْتَحْيِي نِسَاءَهُمْ ۚ

201
00:15:22,326 --> 00:15:26,332
So, he kills the sons and he lets the females live.

202
00:15:26,559 --> 00:15:30,428
إِنَّهُ كَانَ مِنَ الْمُفْسِدِينَ۝

203
00:15:30,462 --> 00:15:33,542
He was of those who commit great sins and crimes.

204
00:15:33,715 --> 00:15:34,702
And then Allah says;

205
00:15:35,195 --> 00:15:41,241
وَنُرِيدُ أَن نَّمُنَّ عَلَى الَّذِينَ اسْتُضْعِفُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ

206
00:15:41,421 --> 00:15:47,060
وَنَجْعَلَهُمْ أَئِمَّةً وَنَجْعَلَهُمُ الْوَارِثِينَ۝

207
00:15:47,123 --> 00:15:48,096
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says;

208
00:15:48,263 --> 00:15:57,032
And We wish to do a favor to those who are weak in the land and to make them rulers and to make them the inheritors.

209
00:15:57,626 --> 00:16:03,412
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wants and Firaon(فرعون) wants, but whatever Allah wills will pass.

210
00:16:03,912 --> 00:16:06,530
Allah wanted to give his favourite to the weak nation.

211
00:16:06,770 --> 00:16:10,730
Allah wanted to bring that weak nation from the bottom and put them on the top.

212
00:16:12,076 --> 00:16:13,340
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

213
00:16:13,460 --> 00:16:15,007
وَنُمَكِّنَ لَهُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ

214
00:16:15,207 --> 00:16:16,887
And to establish them in the land,

215
00:16:17,067 --> 00:16:27,611
وَنُمَكِّنَ لَهُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَنُرِيَ فِرْعَوْنَ وَهَامَانَ وَجُنُودَهُمَا مِنْهُم مَّا كَانُوا يَحْذَرُونَ۝

216
00:16:27,874 --> 00:16:34,483
And We let Firaon(فرعون) and Haman(هامان) their hosts receive from them that which they feared.

217
00:16:34,983 --> 00:16:41,317
Some of the Sahabah رضى الله عنهم said that, Firaon(فرعون) saw a dream.

218
00:16:42,084 --> 00:16:49,502
He saw a dream where there is a light coming out from the Holy Land, Jerusalem(يروشلم)

219
00:16:50,128 --> 00:17:02,708
and this light or fire والله اعلم swept through Egypt and it destroyed everyone except for the Houses of the children of Israel(اسرائيل).

220
00:17:04,548 --> 00:17:07,358
So he asked for the interpretation of this dream.

221
00:17:07,840 --> 00:17:10,513
He was told that it means that

222
00:17:10,663 --> 00:17:20,736
there will be a man from the children of Israel(اسرائيل) who will take away your kingdom from you;

223
00:17:21,403 --> 00:17:26,322
and will destroy your army and your people.

224
00:17:27,008 --> 00:17:28,655
This was the interpretation of the dream.

225
00:17:29,468 --> 00:17:32,673
So, he said for Firaon(فرعون) it was easy, simple.

226
00:17:33,820 --> 00:17:40,487
He gave his orders to kill every child who was born in the houses Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

227
00:17:41,430 --> 00:17:51,278
And it says that he would send out spies, his security agents, to go and find out any woman of the children of Israel who's pregnant

228
00:17:51,334 --> 00:17:55,468
and they would put her under surveillance before she even gives birth.

229
00:17:56,001 --> 00:17:57,992
And they would put her under surveillance

230
00:17:58,379 --> 00:18:02,692
and as soon as she delivers; if it's a boy, they would slaughter him.

231
00:18:03,266 --> 00:18:06,306
And if it's a girl, they would let her live.

232
00:18:07,170 --> 00:18:09,437
  يُذَبِّحُ أَبْنَاءَهُمْ وَيَسْتَحْيِي نِسَاءَهُمْ ۚ

233
00:18:09,617 --> 00:18:12,757
He kills the males and he allows the females live.

234
00:18:13,984 --> 00:18:18,860
The mother of Musa(موسى) became pregnant,

235
00:18:19,254 --> 00:18:21,045
but she concealed her pregnancy.

236
00:18:22,365 --> 00:18:30,219
No matter how strong the security forces and the spying agency is, they are always going to miss something.

237
00:18:30,946 --> 00:18:33,293
There is some information they're going to overlook.

238
00:18:34,393 --> 00:18:39,835
So, in this particular case, in the situation of the mother of Musa(موسى), they did not notice her pregnancy.

239
00:18:41,375 --> 00:18:45,402
So she was able to conceal her pregnancy until she delivered

240
00:18:47,115 --> 00:18:54,687
and when she delivered Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى) now it's even more difficult to hide the fact.

241
00:18:55,274 --> 00:19:01,320
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told the mother of Musa عليه السلام.

242
00:19:01,760 --> 00:19:03,660
وَأَوْحَيْنَا إِلَىٰ أُمِّ مُوسَىٰ

243
00:19:04,440 --> 00:19:07,133
Now this is not Wahi(وحى) of Nabuwah(نبوة).

244
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:14,286
The word Wahi(وحى) could mean either inspiration or it could mean revelation to a Nabi(نَبِي).

245
00:19:15,070 --> 00:19:19,236
In this particular situation, it is inspiration; Ilham(الهام).

246
00:19:19,449 --> 00:19:21,436
It is not revelation to a Nabi(نَبِي).

247
00:19:22,376 --> 00:19:28,729
Because when the word Wahi(وحى) is mentioned in Qur'an doesn't necessarily have to mean, revelation of a Nabi(نَبِي)

248
00:19:28,759 --> 00:19:32,422
because, we have a place in Qur'an where Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says in surat-ul-Nahl(سورة النحل);

249
00:19:32,595 --> 00:19:34,194
وَأَوْحَىٰ رَبُّكَ إِلَى النَّحْلِ

250
00:19:34,495 --> 00:19:36,733
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; We revealed to the bees,

251
00:19:36,763 --> 00:19:37,893
so are the bees prophets.?

252
00:19:38,759 --> 00:19:41,906
So this revelation over here means inspiration.

253
00:19:42,826 --> 00:19:45,812
It's the strongest inspiration in the heart of the mother of Musa(موسى).

254
00:19:45,945 --> 00:19:47,745
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is telling her;

255
00:19:48,132 --> 00:19:55,487
وَأَوْحَيْنَا إِلَىٰ أُمِّ مُوسَىٰ أَنْ أَرْضِعِيهِ ۖ

256
00:19:55,727 --> 00:20:03,438
فَإِذَا خِفْتِ عَلَيْهِ فَأَلْقِيهِ فِي الْيَمِّ وَلَا تَخَافِي وَلَا تَحْزَنِي ۖ

257
00:20:03,611 --> 00:20:11,717
إِنَّا رَادُّوهُ إِلَيْكِ وَجَاعِلُوهُ مِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ۝

258
00:20:11,803 --> 00:20:13,185
 Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said;

259
00:20:13,457 --> 00:20:16,663
And We inspired the mother of Musa(موسى) saying;

260
00:20:16,897 --> 00:20:18,583
Suckle him breastfeed him.

261
00:20:18,997 --> 00:20:25,604
But when you fear for him, then cast him into the river and fear not nor grief.

262
00:20:26,711 --> 00:20:33,539
Now, this is a strong inspiration, because no mother would throw her child in a flowing river.

263
00:20:34,719 --> 00:20:41,947
And for any of you have seen the Nile River, it's a very, very powerful and strong River.

264
00:20:43,967 --> 00:20:50,020
I mean, people who swim there put themselves at risk of drowning; strong swimmers.

265
00:20:50,460 --> 00:20:53,581
Because it's a very violent and strong moving current.

266
00:20:55,028 --> 00:20:56,712
So this is a very strong inspiration;

267
00:20:56,742 --> 00:21:02,778
because no mother would do this; unless, she has a very strong feeling that this is a command from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

268
00:21:05,051 --> 00:21:09,711
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told her to breastfeed him; breastfeed him as usual.

269
00:21:11,078 --> 00:21:18,812
But whenever you feel danger on him, throw him in what seems to be the biggest danger; the river.

270
00:21:21,325 --> 00:21:25,146
Putting the child in the age of Musa(موسى) might be a few days old;

271
00:21:25,393 --> 00:21:30,100
a baby who can barely see; cannot do himself any good.

272
00:21:31,027 --> 00:21:33,974
And you put him in a river in a wooden box.

273
00:21:35,313 --> 00:21:42,285
That would seem to our limited minds and rational and thinking that, that is throwing him to death.

274
00:21:44,298 --> 00:21:46,951
But because it's an order from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى,

275
00:21:47,036 --> 00:21:54,780
this righteous mother was able to suppress her strong feelings of motherhood and care for the child

276
00:21:55,517 --> 00:22:02,708
and to trust the child in the hands of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and to believe that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى will take care of the child more than her.

277
00:22:04,281 --> 00:22:07,991
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى in this verse is telling her;

278
00:22:08,191 --> 00:22:13,885
Do not fear nor grief; Don't have fear and don't have grief.

279
00:22:14,474 --> 00:22:20,119
We shall bring him back to you and We will make him one of our messengers.

280
00:22:21,740 --> 00:22:30,681
By the way, this Ayah(آية) it has two do's and don'ts and two pieces of good news.

281
00:22:30,914 --> 00:22:33,251
In this Ayah(آية) there are two orders.

282
00:22:34,878 --> 00:22:39,002
أَرْضِعِيهِ فَإِذَا خِفْتِ عَلَيْهِ فَأَلْقِيهِ فِي الْيَمِّ۝

283
00:22:39,108 --> 00:22:44,540
Breastfeed him; and if you have fear on him, then throw him in the river.

284
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:51,142
And, this shows you the Bulagha(بلاغه) the beauty of the Qur'an, how in one verse you could have all of these different aspects of language.

285
00:22:51,309 --> 00:22:52,436
So these are two orders;

286
00:22:52,636 --> 00:22:56,341
Breastfeed and throw him or put him in the river.

287
00:22:56,652 --> 00:22:59,388
And then there are two don'ts where it says,

288
00:22:59,608 --> 00:23:01,735
وَلَا تَخَافِي وَلَا تَحْزَنِي ۖ

289
00:23:01,901 --> 00:23:05,310
Don't have any fear and don't have any sorrow.

290
00:23:05,664 --> 00:23:07,537
And then it has two promises in it.

291
00:23:07,770 --> 00:23:09,124
إِنَّا رَادُّوهُ إِلَيْكِ

292
00:23:09,210 --> 00:23:10,970
We will return him unto you.

293
00:23:11,211 --> 00:23:14,157
وَجَاعِلُوهُ مِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ۝

294
00:23:14,287 --> 00:23:16,531
And we will make him of the messengers.

295
00:23:17,404 --> 00:23:22,115
So it has two promises to the mother of Musa(موسى); we are going to bring him back to you; Don't worry

296
00:23:22,695 --> 00:23:24,968
and he's going to be of the messengers.

297
00:23:25,281 --> 00:23:29,176
This is a very strong test from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى for this righteous mother.

298
00:23:30,523 --> 00:23:32,703
If you care for your child throw him in the river.

299
00:23:34,476 --> 00:23:43,026
So, she breastfed Musa(موسى), she put him in a wooden casket; in a wooden box

300
00:23:44,197 --> 00:23:51,472
and she put him in the Nile River and she let her child go in front of her eyes.

301
00:23:53,771 --> 00:23:57,891
Just to fulfill this inspiration and promise of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى,

302
00:23:58,324 --> 00:24:03,705
where Allah is telling her; We are going to return him to you and we are going to make him of the messengers.

303
00:24:05,378 --> 00:24:13,633
This mother fulfill the two promises of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى or fulfill the commandment of Allah to receive these promises.

304
00:24:14,053 --> 00:24:15,873
How many promises do we have?

305
00:24:16,986 --> 00:24:19,974
Nevertheless, we're not acting upon the orders of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

306
00:24:20,558 --> 00:24:25,002
We are told that if we're going to strive and struggle in Jihad(جهاد) in the sake of Allah, Allah is going to give us victory.

307
00:24:25,047 --> 00:24:25,770
We're not doing that.

308
00:24:25,894 --> 00:24:29,405
We are told if you spend in the sake of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, Allah is going to give you more.

309
00:24:29,435 --> 00:24:30,126
We don't do that.

310
00:24:30,456 --> 00:24:33,613
We are told that if we have tawakul(توكل) in Allahسُبحانه وتعالى

311
00:24:33,643 --> 00:24:35,156
Allah is going to provide for us more.

312
00:24:35,340 --> 00:24:36,066
We don't do that.

313
00:24:36,340 --> 00:24:41,260
We are told if we have Taqwa(تقوى) Allah is going to provide us with Rizq(رزق) from sources we don't know.

314
00:24:41,413 --> 00:24:44,823
وَمَن يَتَّقِ اللَّهَ يَجْعَل لَّهُ مَخْرَجًا ۝ وَيَرْزُقْهُ مِنْ حَيْثُ لَا يَحْتَسِبُ

315
00:24:45,006 --> 00:24:45,999
And we don't do that.

316
00:24:46,865 --> 00:24:49,027
The mother of Musa(موسى) did this;

317
00:24:49,223 --> 00:24:55,651
Even though, it is much more difficult for her to do it because she's a mother and this is her child a few days old,

318
00:24:55,784 --> 00:25:00,056
and she was ordered, a drastic and very difficult thing to do.

319
00:25:00,229 --> 00:25:03,663
And that is to put him in the Nile River; But she did it.

320
00:25:04,282 --> 00:25:07,012
And we are going to see the results of her actions.

321
00:25:08,059 --> 00:25:12,745
We're going to see what happens when you fulfill the order of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

322
00:25:12,872 --> 00:25:16,632
We're going to see how Allah fulfills his promises unto you.

323
00:25:17,858 --> 00:25:26,554
When this wooden box was sent in the river; it kept on flowing through the Nile River.

324
00:25:27,514 --> 00:25:29,507
The waves are moving it around.

325
00:25:30,167 --> 00:25:35,870
And there are many houses and communities on this Nile River.

326
00:25:35,930 --> 00:25:41,341
I mean, all of the people of Egypt were living on that river; that was their livelihood.

327
00:25:42,241 --> 00:25:44,108
Egypt is desert, there's no rain.

328
00:25:44,434 --> 00:25:48,105
The people are living on the water of the Nile River.

329
00:25:48,352 --> 00:25:50,634
So that is where all of the communities of Egypt are;

330
00:25:50,664 --> 00:26:00,340
Even until this day; you rarely find communities living on the west or the east flanks of the river; everybody is surrounding this river.

331
00:26:01,034 --> 00:26:06,407
So it is their houses lining up around the Nile River.

332
00:26:06,673 --> 00:26:08,620
This wooden casket is moving.

333
00:26:09,053 --> 00:26:17,958
And out of every house; Out of all of the houses lining up on the west and the east side of the river.

334
00:26:18,191 --> 00:26:22,091
Where does this wooden box choose to park?

335
00:26:24,324 --> 00:26:26,971
All of the people of Egypt are living on this river.

336
00:26:27,957 --> 00:26:31,911
This wooden box is swimming through the waves of the Nile River.

337
00:26:32,457 --> 00:26:37,070
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is directing it and guiding it and navigating it through this river.

338
00:26:37,584 --> 00:26:44,836
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى sends this wooden box right on the shores of the palace of Firaon(فرعون).

339
00:26:48,029 --> 00:26:54,999
The mother of Musa(موسى) threw this child in the Nile River to get him away from Firaon(فرعون).

340
00:26:55,872 --> 00:26:59,812
To get him away from Firaon(فرعون); That's why she put him in the river; in the first place.

341
00:27:00,092 --> 00:27:02,948
So that, the child can run away from Firaon(فرعون);

342
00:27:03,428 --> 00:27:08,755
But Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wants this baby and child to go right to the palace of Firaon(فرعون).

343
00:27:10,562 --> 00:27:14,316
And if the mother of Musa(موسى) was watching this; she's going to say what promise is this?

344
00:27:14,346 --> 00:27:21,096
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى promised me that He's going to save my child for me, and then my child goes and parks right next to the palace of Firaon(فرعون)?

345
00:27:21,590 --> 00:27:23,220
But her Eeman(ايمان) was firm.

346
00:27:23,506 --> 00:27:24,830
رَّبَطْنَا عَلَىٰ قَلْبِهَا

347
00:27:24,860 --> 00:27:29,072
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; We tied her heart firm with Eeman(ايمان).

348
00:27:30,838 --> 00:27:33,243
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has a plan.

349
00:27:34,069 --> 00:27:35,486
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

350
00:27:35,516 --> 00:27:41,542
فَالْتَقَطَهُ آلُ فِرْعَوْنَ لِيَكُونَ لَهُمْ عَدُوًّا وَحَزَنًا

351
00:27:43,088 --> 00:27:45,035
This is the plan of Allah; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

352
00:27:45,209 --> 00:27:54,583
Then the household of Firaon(فرعون) picked him up, that he might become for them an enemy and the cause of grief.

353
00:27:55,883 --> 00:27:57,862
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has a plan.

354
00:27:58,709 --> 00:28:07,673
Allah wants them To pick up Musa(موسى); so that, he will be grieve for them and he would be their enemy.

355
00:28:09,127 --> 00:28:13,855
And how could that work out; We have no way of understanding.

356
00:28:14,933 --> 00:28:19,735
Because this is a mystery of the omnipotence of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and his Qudrah(قدره).

357
00:28:19,793 --> 00:28:21,760
The Qudrah(قدره) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and His ability.

358
00:28:22,353 --> 00:28:30,348
How could Musa(موسى) end up being the grieve for Firaon(فرعون), when he will be raised up in the palace of Firaon(فرعون)?

359
00:28:31,501 --> 00:28:32,474
So, they picked him up.

360
00:28:32,541 --> 00:28:33,374
What happened is?

361
00:28:33,787 --> 00:28:39,956
Some soldiers or servents; they saw this box; they opened it up; they found the child in there; where did they take it.

362
00:28:39,986 --> 00:28:46,116
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wants that child not to land in the hands of Firaon(فرعون), but to land in the hands of the wife of Firaon(فرعون); Asiyah(آسيه).

363
00:28:47,310 --> 00:28:51,736
So Asiyah(آسيه) picked up this wooden box and saw this baby in it.

364
00:28:52,143 --> 00:28:55,813
This child, she fell in love with him.

365
00:28:56,280 --> 00:29:04,168
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى put the love of this righteous baby in the heart of this righteous woman.

366
00:29:05,394 --> 00:29:06,388
She said;

367
00:29:07,248 --> 00:29:12,653
وَقَالَتِ امْرَأَتُ فِرْعَوْنَ قُرَّتُ عَيْنٍ لِّي وَلَكَ ۖ لَا تَقْتُلُوهُ

368
00:29:14,471 --> 00:29:20,369
She said; A comfort of the eye for me and for you; kill him not.

369
00:29:21,016 --> 00:29:24,996
So we kind of sense here that, maybe Firaon(فرعون) wanted to kill this child.

370
00:29:25,956 --> 00:29:28,421
Because, the wife of Firaon(فرعون) was saying; Don't kill him.

371
00:29:29,541 --> 00:29:32,400
So maybe there was an attempt to kill Musa(موسى).

372
00:29:33,340 --> 00:29:36,686
I mean, Firaon(فرعون) was killing right and left all of the children of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

373
00:29:36,900 --> 00:29:41,271
So he might have felt there's a possibility; this could be from the children of Israel(اسرائيل); why not get rid of him.

374
00:29:42,244 --> 00:29:49,444
But Allahسُبحانه وتعالى put some support for Musa(موسى) in the palace of Firaon(فرعون).

375
00:29:50,741 --> 00:29:53,768
See, when Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wants to help His servants;

376
00:29:54,061 --> 00:29:58,201
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ can; You don't know who the soldiers of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى are.

377
00:29:58,552 --> 00:30:06,366
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى put an insider in the palace of Firaon(فرعون); to support Syedina Musa عليه السلام.

378
00:30:07,498 --> 00:30:11,784
And that is the wife of Firaon(فرعون); She's an insider, she's the queen.

379
00:30:12,277 --> 00:30:15,801
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى made her a supporter of Musa(موسى).

380
00:30:16,622 --> 00:30:18,088
Just like in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ);

381
00:30:18,748 --> 00:30:24,452
When the non-believers surrounded the Muslims in a Sha'ab(شعب) and they boycotted them for three years.

382
00:30:24,792 --> 00:30:29,412
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى put in the hearts of some of the strong men of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

383
00:30:30,032 --> 00:30:34,775
The intention of breaking up this embargo; even though, they were non Muslims.

384
00:30:35,715 --> 00:30:41,068
But Allahسُبحانه وتعالى can use anyone who wants for the sake of His religion.

385
00:30:41,442 --> 00:30:42,652
Even if, they're non Muslim;

386
00:30:43,119 --> 00:30:47,899
Even if, they intend to be enemies of Islam; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى can use their actions against them.

387
00:30:49,179 --> 00:30:55,169
So we should always have trust in Allahسُبحانه وتعالى that no matter how the enemy is strong;

388
00:30:55,356 --> 00:30:59,808
No matter how powerful the devil's work seems to be.

389
00:30:59,994 --> 00:31:05,348
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى can provide us with victory, if we fulfill the requirements of victory.

390
00:31:05,661 --> 00:31:07,074
إِن تَنصُرُوا اللَّهَ يَنصُرْكُمْ

391
00:31:07,366 --> 00:31:09,726
If you give victory to Allah, Allah will give victory to you.

392
00:31:10,180 --> 00:31:16,669
So, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى provide for the helpless child, an insider to take care of him and that is the wife of Firaon(فرعون).

393
00:31:16,816 --> 00:31:17,195
she said;

394
00:31:17,255 --> 00:31:18,289
قُرَّتُ عَيْنٍ لِّي وَلَكَ

395
00:31:18,749 --> 00:31:23,608
He would be comfort for my eyes and comfort for your eyes

396
00:31:24,008 --> 00:31:27,836
and we will take him as an adopted son; Because they did not have any children.

397
00:31:29,222 --> 00:31:31,090
It is said that Firaon(فرعون) said;

398
00:31:31,230 --> 00:31:35,246
قرة عين لك وليس قرة عين لى

399
00:31:35,939 --> 00:31:39,939
He will be a comfort for your eyes but I don't want him to be comfort for mine.

400
00:31:42,099 --> 00:31:43,735
Actually, he's making Dua(دُعَا) against himself.

401
00:31:43,765 --> 00:31:45,809
He said; I don't want this man to be comfort for my eyes.

402
00:31:46,352 --> 00:31:49,719
Let him be comfort for your eyes; And he was comfort for the eyes of Asiyah(آسيه)

403
00:31:50,065 --> 00:31:52,211
but he was not comfort for the eyes of Firaon(فرعون).

404
00:31:53,011 --> 00:31:55,057
So, these words of Firaon(فرعون) were fulfill.

405
00:31:56,044 --> 00:32:01,152
لَا تَقْتُلُوهُ عَسَىٰ أَن يَنفَعَنَا أَوْ نَتَّخِذَهُ وَلَدًا

406
00:32:01,884 --> 00:32:08,611
Don't kill him; Perhaps, he may be a benefit for us or we may adopt him as a son.

407
00:32:09,491 --> 00:32:11,104
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

408
00:32:11,784 --> 00:32:14,748
وَأَصْبَحَ فُؤَادُ أُمِّ مُوسَىٰ فَارِغًا ۖ

409
00:32:14,778 --> 00:32:17,187
And the heart of the mother of Musa(موسى) became empty;

410
00:32:17,687 --> 00:32:22,009
Look at the expression, her heart was empty; it was completely drained.

411
00:32:22,573 --> 00:32:25,078
Because she does not have her son in her hands.

412
00:32:25,298 --> 00:32:27,218
She does not know where he is.

413
00:32:27,465 --> 00:32:29,512
Her heart was completely drained.

414
00:32:29,985 --> 00:32:30,972
فَارِغًاۖ

415
00:32:31,774 --> 00:32:33,229
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

416
00:32:33,423 --> 00:32:35,369
إِن كَادَتْ لَتُبْدِي بِهِ

417
00:32:35,956 --> 00:32:38,863
She was about to disclose his case.

418
00:32:39,356 --> 00:32:43,908
She was about to go out in the streets of Egypt saying where's my child?

419
00:32:44,988 --> 00:32:48,151
And if she did that; then his case would be exposed,

420
00:32:48,204 --> 00:32:51,265
because it would be known that, he is from the children of Israel(اسرائيل), and he would be killed.

421
00:32:51,998 --> 00:32:53,272
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

422
00:32:53,312 --> 00:32:57,372
لَوْلَا أَن رَّبَطْنَا عَلَىٰ قَلْبِهَا لِتَكُونَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ۝

423
00:32:58,563 --> 00:33:03,222
But we strengthened her heart so that, she might remain as one of the believers.

424
00:33:03,576 --> 00:33:07,475
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى strengthen that empty heart with Eeman(ايمان).

425
00:33:08,315 --> 00:33:11,542
Nothing can fill an empty heart; but Eeman(ايمان).

426
00:33:12,042 --> 00:33:19,283
So, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى filled the heart of the righteous mother of Musa(موسى) with Eeman(ايمان) and that kept her quiet.

427
00:33:19,410 --> 00:33:22,050
She was able to conceal this issue.

428
00:33:22,430 --> 00:33:25,325
She did not speak out about it.

429
00:33:26,192 --> 00:33:30,025
But she told the sister of Musa(موسى); her daughter.

430
00:33:30,451 --> 00:33:34,235
She said; Go and find out, what happened to Musa(موسى)?

431
00:33:34,634 --> 00:33:38,494
When the mother put her baby in the river;

432
00:33:39,948 --> 00:33:46,669
This wooden casket was moving in the Nile River and this sister of Musa(موسى) was following it on the shore.

433
00:33:48,009 --> 00:33:53,818
So, the casket is moving in the river and this girl is running along the river.

434
00:33:54,524 --> 00:33:59,271
So, she knew where the final destination was; She knew that, it was in the Palace of Firaon(فرعون).

435
00:34:01,084 --> 00:34:09,735
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى did not allow Musa(موسى) to suck milk from any breastfeeder.

436
00:34:11,142 --> 00:34:14,215
They brought for him woman to feed him and he would refuse.

437
00:34:15,035 --> 00:34:18,661
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى did not allow Musa(موسى) to drink from anyone.

438
00:34:19,321 --> 00:34:21,355
Because Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has a plan.

439
00:34:22,215 --> 00:34:29,297
So now, Musa(موسى) is in the hands of the queen, but he's refusing to suckle any milk.

440
00:34:29,851 --> 00:34:31,331
He does not want to breastfeed.

441
00:34:32,671 --> 00:34:38,331
And then, the sister of Musa(موسى) arrives and she says;

442
00:34:38,485 --> 00:34:42,541
I can provide you with someone who will breastfeed this child.

443
00:34:45,027 --> 00:34:46,721
She's talking about the mother of Musa(موسى).

444
00:34:47,867 --> 00:34:48,941
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

445
00:34:48,976 --> 00:34:53,510
وَحَرَّمْنَا عَلَيْهِ الْمَرَاضِعَ مِن قَبْلُ

446
00:34:53,616 --> 00:35:02,680
فَقَالَتْ هَلْ أَدُلُّكُمْ عَلَىٰ أَهْلِ بَيْتٍ يَكْفُلُونَهُ لَكُمْ وَهُمْ لَهُ نَاصِحُونَ۝

447
00:35:02,881 --> 00:35:05,927
And she said to his sister; follow him.

448
00:35:06,047 --> 00:35:11,191
So she; his sister watched him from a far place secretly, while they perceived not.

449
00:35:11,458 --> 00:35:16,158
And we had already forbidden other foster suckling mothers for him.

450
00:35:16,364 --> 00:35:21,125
Until, she said; Shall I direct you to a household who will rear him for you.

451
00:35:21,299 --> 00:35:24,659
And sincerely, they will look after him in a good manner?

452
00:35:26,466 --> 00:35:27,933
They said; Okay, we'll try.

453
00:35:28,953 --> 00:35:35,225
They took the child to the mother of Musa(موسى) and immediately, Musa(موسى) started to breastfeed.

454
00:35:36,433 --> 00:35:45,217
Now, the Queen said; I will want you or I'm inviting you to come and breastfeed him in the palace.

455
00:35:45,684 --> 00:35:51,084
But now, the mother of Musa(موسى) has leverage; She has monopoly over this issue.

456
00:35:51,510 --> 00:35:54,626
Nobody else can breastfeed Musa(موسى); but her.

457
00:35:55,165 --> 00:35:56,959
So, she is setting the terms now.

458
00:35:57,333 --> 00:36:01,595
She said; No, I have husband and I have children; I have to take care of them at home.

459
00:36:01,808 --> 00:36:05,455
So, you have to bring the child to me to my house to breastfeed.

460
00:36:07,035 --> 00:36:14,157
Look at this, Musa(موسى); who was dropped in the river alone; by the mother of Musa(موسى),

461
00:36:14,187 --> 00:36:15,700
because of her Eeman(ايمان);

462
00:36:16,820 --> 00:36:27,889
He is now leaving the Palace of Firaon(فرعون) under Royal Guards and going to the house of his parents

463
00:36:28,296 --> 00:36:33,981
and the mother of Musa(موسى) is being paid to take care of her own child.

464
00:36:35,734 --> 00:36:37,941
وَمَن يَتَّقِ اللَّهَ يَجْعَل لَّهُ مَخْرَجًا۝

465
00:36:38,360 --> 00:36:42,464
The one who has Taqwa(تقوى); Allahسُبحانه وتعالى will provide a way out for him.

466
00:36:43,144 --> 00:36:49,089
If the mother of Musa(موسى) did not believe in the promise of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى;

467
00:36:49,596 --> 00:36:54,696
Her child would have been killed; Musa(موسى) would have been killed.

468
00:36:54,749 --> 00:36:59,469
If the mother of Musa(موسى) kept the child with her; he would have been killed.

469
00:37:00,315 --> 00:37:05,223
But because, she believed in the promise of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and she let him go.

470
00:37:05,510 --> 00:37:10,895
Now, Musa(موسى) is protected by the security guards of Firaon(فرعون).

471
00:37:11,261 --> 00:37:18,467
And he became a source of Rizq(رزق) for the whole family, because they're paying her to take care of Musa(موسى).

472
00:37:18,867 --> 00:37:23,900
And the whole family is honored, because they're taking care of the adopted son of Firaon(فرعون).

473
00:37:25,246 --> 00:37:27,120
Look at the result of Taqwa(تقوى).

474
00:37:27,440 --> 00:37:28,833
This is the result of Taqwa(تقوى).

475
00:37:29,153 --> 00:37:32,480
وَمَن يَتَّقِ اللَّهَ يَجْعَل لَّهُ مَخْرَجًا ۝ وَيَرْزُقْهُ مِنْ حَيْثُ لَا يَحْتَسِبُ ۚ

476
00:37:32,568 --> 00:37:39,448
If you have Taqwa(تقوى), Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is going to provide the way out for you, and he's going to provide for you, from sources you perceive not.

477
00:37:40,862 --> 00:37:42,539
فَرَدَدْنَاهُ إِلَىٰ أُمِّهِ

478
00:37:42,866 --> 00:37:44,999
Who's the one who returned Musa(موسى) to his mother?

479
00:37:45,246 --> 00:37:45,946
Allah.

480
00:37:46,253 --> 00:37:47,773
فَرَدَدْنَاهُ إِلَىٰ أُمِّهِ

481
00:37:47,913 --> 00:37:51,468
So, Did We restore him to his mother?

482
00:37:51,795 --> 00:37:54,215
كَيْ تَقَرَّ عَيْنُهَا وَلَا تَحْزَنَ

483
00:37:54,408 --> 00:37:56,348
That, she might be delighted.

484
00:37:56,378 --> 00:37:58,912
Allah wants her to delight her; Allah wants to make her happy.

485
00:37:59,155 --> 00:38:01,338
And that, she might not grieve.

486
00:38:01,637 --> 00:38:03,017
Allah doesn't want her to grieve.

487
00:38:03,451 --> 00:38:05,898
Why? Because of her righteousness and her Taqwa(تقوى).

488
00:38:06,144 --> 00:38:08,358
وَلِتَعْلَمَ أَنَّ وَعْدَ اللَّهِ حَقٌّ

489
00:38:08,505 --> 00:38:11,758
And so that she might know, that the promise of Allah is true.

490
00:38:11,918 --> 00:38:14,405
وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ۝

491
00:38:14,535 --> 00:38:16,612
But most of them know not.

492
00:38:16,911 --> 00:38:20,431
Most of the people do not know that the promise of Allah is true.

493
00:38:21,272 --> 00:38:24,365
Unfortunately, we all say; we believe in the promise of Allah.

494
00:38:24,612 --> 00:38:28,905
We say that, but it's lip service; Deep in our hearts, we don't act that way.

495
00:38:30,031 --> 00:38:31,837
وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ۝

496
00:38:31,875 --> 00:38:33,328
Most of the people do not know this.

497
00:38:33,364 --> 00:38:36,501
And when Allah says this; it means, they don't act upon that.

498
00:38:36,621 --> 00:38:39,108
They might say that, they believe in the promise of Allah

499
00:38:39,154 --> 00:38:46,043
but who acts upon that and who fulfills these commandments of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to receive the promise of Allah.

500
00:38:47,617 --> 00:38:49,914
I think this part of the story of Musa(موسى);

501
00:38:50,221 --> 00:38:56,379
If we think about it, it is an example of the ultimate level of weakness.

502
00:38:57,325 --> 00:39:01,892
When you depend on Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; no matter how weak you are;

503
00:39:02,359 --> 00:39:05,880
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى can provide you with the most strength.

504
00:39:07,447 --> 00:39:13,351
Because Bannu Israel(بنو أسرائيل) were helpless and Musa(موسى) was a helpless child.

505
00:39:14,271 --> 00:39:18,738
But the Allahسُبحانه وتعالى provided for him protection from all sources.

506
00:39:19,884 --> 00:39:24,078
Our Ummah(امة) is in a similar situation now; we are in a very, very weak state.

507
00:39:25,305 --> 00:39:32,499
If we would put our trust in Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, Allah is going to protect us from sources, we perceive not.

508
00:39:33,139 --> 00:39:37,186
Because no way could the mother of Musa(موسى) have imagined; what will happen.

509
00:39:37,826 --> 00:39:44,482
No way, could anyone, decode the plan of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى

510
00:39:44,512 --> 00:39:51,653
and understand the mystery of the ability of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and how the plan of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى works.

511
00:39:53,239 --> 00:39:58,636
Musa(موسى) is being raised up in the palace of Firaon(فرعون) and he's receiving the best treatment;

512
00:39:58,829 --> 00:40:00,389
Because he's their adopted son.

513
00:40:01,316 --> 00:40:05,229
Musa(موسى) grew up in the palace of Firaon(فرعون).

514
00:40:05,849 --> 00:40:07,363
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

515
00:40:07,609 --> 00:40:16,287
وَلَمَّا بَلَغَ أَشُدَّهُ آتَيْنَاهُ حُكْمًا وَعِلْمًا

516
00:40:16,527 --> 00:40:20,014
وَكَذَلِكَ نَجْزِي الْمُحْسِنِينَ۝

517
00:40:20,177 --> 00:40:28,154
And when he attained his full strength and was perfect in manhood, We bestowed on him,

518
00:40:28,954 --> 00:40:30,677
حُكْمًا وَعِلْمًا

519
00:40:31,437 --> 00:40:35,653
Hukum(حكم) is the good and right judgment Ilm(علم) is knowledge.

520
00:40:35,717 --> 00:40:41,152
And we talked about the importance of these two, when we were talking about SadyinaYusuf(سَيِّدنا يوسُف).

521
00:40:41,825 --> 00:40:42,878
حُكْمًا وَعِلْمًا

522
00:40:43,058 --> 00:40:48,325
Allah gave the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء)  both; not knowledge alone and not the judgment alone.

523
00:40:48,505 --> 00:40:55,399
Allah gave them good judgment and knowledge together, because these two things work together to form the complete personality.

524
00:40:56,447 --> 00:40:58,281
وَكَذَلِكَ نَجْزِي الْمُحْسِنِينَ۝

525
00:40:58,378 --> 00:41:00,294
And thus, do we reward the righteous.

526
00:41:00,981 --> 00:41:06,983
So, Musa(موسى) was described by Rasool Allah ﷺ as being a very large and well built person.

527
00:41:07,273 --> 00:41:11,933
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; he was very dark skin, and his hair was curly.

528
00:41:12,280 --> 00:41:17,800
These were the descriptions of Musa(موسى) and he had a very strong presence and personality.

529
00:41:18,546 --> 00:41:21,755
These are the descriptions of Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى) in the Hadith(حديث).

530
00:41:22,355 --> 00:41:25,348
Musa(موسى) entered into the town; one day.

531
00:41:25,822 --> 00:41:27,419
عَلَىٰ حِينِ غَفْلَةٍ مِّنْ أَهْلِهَا

532
00:41:27,449 --> 00:41:30,136
Allah says; When the people were unaware.

533
00:41:30,529 --> 00:41:33,582
This could have been at noon time or at night time;

534
00:41:34,229 --> 00:41:36,820
The streets were empty; There weren't a lot of people around.

535
00:41:37,907 --> 00:41:39,807
Musa(موسى) saw two men fighting.

536
00:41:41,240 --> 00:41:43,711
And we would see throughout the story of Musa(موسى),

537
00:41:43,771 --> 00:41:51,296
that Musa(موسى) was the type of personality that would not let mistakes pass in front of his eyes, without him intervening.

538
00:41:52,263 --> 00:41:57,863
He had a personality where if, he sees something wrong, he can't let it pass by.

539
00:41:58,063 --> 00:42:00,853
He has to do something; He has to intervene.

540
00:42:01,640 --> 00:42:03,753
So Musa(موسى) saw these two men fighting.

541
00:42:03,907 --> 00:42:05,405
He came to see what's happening.

542
00:42:05,578 --> 00:42:12,206
He saw that one of them, is from his people; the children of Israel(اسرائيل) and the other one was an Egyptian

543
00:42:12,672 --> 00:42:14,119
and they were fighting together.

544
00:42:14,532 --> 00:42:21,134
So Musa(موسى) intervene, to support the Israilite against the Egyptian.

545
00:42:22,114 --> 00:42:23,561
What he did is;

546
00:42:24,087 --> 00:42:25,767
Musa(موسى) had the stick in his hand.

547
00:42:26,487 --> 00:42:30,481
So he pushed the Egyptian with his stick; He just pushed him.

548
00:42:32,028 --> 00:42:33,541
The man fell down; dead.

549
00:42:35,208 --> 00:42:36,341
Musa(موسى) was strong.

550
00:42:37,221 --> 00:42:40,971
Musa(موسى) did not intend to kill; he did not intend to kill.

551
00:42:41,518 --> 00:42:44,031
This was unintentional murder.

552
00:42:44,305 --> 00:42:48,311
But he pushed the man, it was a little bit strong, so the man fell down; dead.

553
00:42:49,831 --> 00:42:59,445
The next day, Musa(موسى) came in the town and he saw the same man from Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) fighting with another Egyptian.

554
00:43:00,045 --> 00:43:05,531
The next day, he already picked up another Fight; troublemaker; He's looking for trouble.

555
00:43:07,314 --> 00:43:10,898
Now, Musa(موسى) rushed ahead.

556
00:43:11,858 --> 00:43:14,289
Musa(موسى) this time, when he rushed ahead,

557
00:43:14,956 --> 00:43:20,778
the man from the children of Israel(اسرائيل), thought that Musa(موسى) this time is going to hit him.

558
00:43:21,244 --> 00:43:29,092
So he said, he backed away and he said; Do you want to kill me, like you've killed somebody yesterday?

559
00:43:30,032 --> 00:43:33,626
Until that moment, nobody knew that Musa(موسى) is the one; who killed the Egyptian.

560
00:43:34,746 --> 00:43:40,945
And now this Israelite, leaked the word out in front of the other man, because the other Egyptian was there.

561
00:43:41,220 --> 00:43:45,435
He told Musa(موسى), Do you want to kill me, like you've killed somebody yesterday?

562
00:43:46,088 --> 00:43:53,715
Now, this wasn't a regular or usual homicide; a crime of murder.

563
00:43:54,399 --> 00:43:56,712
This was a big issue.

564
00:43:57,419 --> 00:43:59,699
And it may be headlines all over Egypt.

565
00:44:00,799 --> 00:44:02,669
Because it was a political issue.

566
00:44:03,742 --> 00:44:11,957
Because it was a dispute between an Egyptian and a member of the weak community; Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل);

567
00:44:12,238 --> 00:44:14,031
The oppressed and the enslaved.

568
00:44:14,471 --> 00:44:21,813
So how can someone from the low class kill someone from the high class?

569
00:44:22,279 --> 00:44:29,611
Because by now, it was already known that Musa(موسى) was from Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) as some of the Mufassireen(مفسرين) say,

570
00:44:29,704 --> 00:44:34,395
but anyway, even if it wasn't the case; it was a big issue.

571
00:44:35,115 --> 00:44:44,395
And it was so big that Firaon(فرعون) and his government met together and his counsel; they met together to discuss this issue.

572
00:44:45,221 --> 00:44:46,846
That is how big it was.

573
00:44:47,266 --> 00:44:49,806
It wasn't an issue that would just go to court; No.

574
00:44:49,986 --> 00:44:56,841
It went all the way up to Firaon(فرعون) and his cabinet and his counsel and they met together to discuss this issue.

575
00:44:58,821 --> 00:45:05,828
Because for them, this was an issue of what? it wasn't Regular murder; it was an issue of terrorism.

576
00:45:07,961 --> 00:45:12,703
It was a terrorist act; That is what this issue was.

577
00:45:13,190 --> 00:45:19,041
Because a Muslim has killed a member of the non Muslim community.

578
00:45:19,274 --> 00:45:24,354
So it's not dealt with the same way they would deal with other crimes which are similar; No.

579
00:45:24,488 --> 00:45:30,319
Because this was committed by a Muslim; It has to be classified as terrorism.

580
00:45:31,059 --> 00:45:40,171
So it was an issue that was discussed by Firaon(فرعون) and his cabinet and the government to fight terrorism through their anti Terrorism Task Force.

581
00:45:40,731 --> 00:45:43,844
So they decided that they have to kill Musa(موسى).

582
00:45:44,883 --> 00:45:51,650
What happened is, that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى made this news leak out through one members of the community.

583
00:45:51,910 --> 00:45:57,709
So he came from the other end of town rushing to convey the news to Musa(موسى), and to tell him;

584
00:45:57,739 --> 00:46:00,029
إِنَّ الْمَلَأَ يَأْتَمِرُونَ بِكَ لِيَقْتُلُوكَ

585
00:46:00,860 --> 00:46:07,485
The leaders are making a plan to kill you; So you better leave immediately.

586
00:46:08,085 --> 00:46:13,096
So Musa(موسى) was told afore time, that he will be killed.

587
00:46:14,896 --> 00:46:20,628
I just want to add one thing about this man from Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

588
00:46:22,021 --> 00:46:26,535
When Musa(موسى) saw him causing trouble again, What did he tell him?

589
00:46:26,708 --> 00:46:27,416
He told him;

590
00:46:28,232 --> 00:46:29,795
إِنَّكَ لَغَوِيٌّ مُّبِينٌ۝

591
00:46:29,819 --> 00:46:31,332
He said; you are a plane misleader.

592
00:46:31,678 --> 00:46:33,412
Because, he was causing too much trouble.

593
00:46:34,312 --> 00:46:36,903
When Musa(موسى) told him; you are a plane misleader.

594
00:46:37,857 --> 00:46:43,510
The Israelite interpreted this as Musa(موسى) wanting to attack him.

595
00:46:44,110 --> 00:46:45,801
He thought that Musa(موسى) is going to attack him.

596
00:46:46,695 --> 00:46:53,930
So when Musa(موسى) was moving ahead, he said; you want to kill me just like you have killed someone the day before.

597
00:46:54,790 --> 00:46:56,577
Who did Musa(موسى) help the day before?

598
00:46:57,364 --> 00:46:58,584
He helped this man.

599
00:46:59,324 --> 00:47:07,872
The next day, the man was willing to betray Musa(موسى), who just saved him; the day before.

600
00:47:08,552 --> 00:47:12,144
Musa(موسى) did this man a favor; he helped him and supported him.

601
00:47:12,531 --> 00:47:19,801
The next day this man betrayed Musa(موسى) and disclosed the secret that happened the day before.

602
00:47:20,234 --> 00:47:21,854
This shows you something.

603
00:47:22,488 --> 00:47:27,568
It shows you some of the qualities of people who are humiliated and oppressed.

604
00:47:28,787 --> 00:47:34,645
When people and societies go under oppression and humiliation for a long time;

605
00:47:35,065 --> 00:47:39,023
they become very weak personalities and they become very selfish.

606
00:47:40,036 --> 00:47:44,323
You find that people who are living under oppression, are very selfish people.

607
00:47:45,175 --> 00:47:50,113
If they have been undergoing oppression for a very long time and they do nothing to stop it.

608
00:47:50,573 --> 00:47:53,346
You can find that the reason is because they are selfish.

609
00:47:53,406 --> 00:47:55,680
Everybody's saying; myself!, myself!.

610
00:47:56,740 --> 00:48:01,347
Because if they were considering the community.

611
00:48:01,613 --> 00:48:03,705
The oppression wouldn't continue; they would stop it.

612
00:48:04,980 --> 00:48:09,738
But these people are going through this oppression continuously and suffering the humiliation;

613
00:48:09,927 --> 00:48:15,173
Because they don't want to work together; They are selfish and everyone is looking at his own benefit and gain.

614
00:48:16,091 --> 00:48:21,619
So this man is an example, is a representation of people who are humiliated.

615
00:48:21,959 --> 00:48:24,593
And these are the type of people that Musa(موسى) have had to deal with.

616
00:48:25,046 --> 00:48:30,503
He had to deal with people who lived under the oppression and the tyranny of Firaon(فرعون) for a very, very long time.

617
00:48:30,996 --> 00:48:36,750
See their whole personality; see people when they go under long periods of oppression, they lose dignity.

618
00:48:37,256 --> 00:48:41,784
See this man doesn't have any dignity; He doesn't care if he betrays.

619
00:48:41,997 --> 00:48:44,834
As long as, he's going to save his life; he'll do anything.

620
00:48:44,974 --> 00:48:46,701
They lose the dignity and honor.

621
00:48:47,041 --> 00:48:51,674
And honorable and dignified person is not going to do this to somebody, who did him a favor.

622
00:48:51,874 --> 00:48:55,561
He's going to be grateful and he's willing to die to help Musa(موسى).

623
00:48:56,114 --> 00:49:02,711
He's willing to sacrifice his life to support Musa(موسى) rather than betray Musa(موسى) and cause him all of this suffering and pain.

624
00:49:04,231 --> 00:49:08,104
And that could happen to the Muslim Ummah(امة) today.

625
00:49:08,431 --> 00:49:11,127
If we do not stop the oppression that our Ummah(امة) is going through.

626
00:49:11,554 --> 00:49:14,474
This is the type of personalities that we're going to reap in the end.

627
00:49:15,941 --> 00:49:22,988
Musa(موسى) did not have any time to prepare his belongings and his luggage; He had to immediately flee out of Egypt.

628
00:49:23,648 --> 00:49:26,468
And he headed east; That's the way to get out.

629
00:49:26,808 --> 00:49:28,849
And he immediately rushed out of Egypt.

630
00:49:29,282 --> 00:49:35,056
There was no time to do anything, because the warrant for his arrest was already out.

631
00:49:35,602 --> 00:49:37,128
So he had to leave immediately.

632
00:49:37,542 --> 00:49:42,022
So he left out of Egypt to the direction of the east.

633
00:49:42,522 --> 00:49:45,784
And he traveled all the way; out of Egypt.

634
00:49:46,257 --> 00:49:51,104
It is said that; he had shoes on; He kept on walking, until his shoes were torn apart.

635
00:49:51,704 --> 00:49:55,648
And then he was walking on his barefoot, until his skin peeled out.

636
00:49:56,455 --> 00:49:58,675
And he would eat whatever he would find.

637
00:49:58,735 --> 00:50:05,877
He was eating the leaves of the trees until, the surrounding his lips was a green layer;

638
00:50:06,010 --> 00:50:10,583
Because of the dryness and the harshness of the leaves of trees; It came out from his mouth.

639
00:50:11,176 --> 00:50:18,023
And he was alone with no food, no supporter, no friends, no family and he kept on walking to the east.

640
00:50:18,356 --> 00:50:23,815
Because he doesn't know; how far he needs to move to get out of Egypt.

641
00:50:24,642 --> 00:50:28,622
Until he arrived to an area called Madyan(مَدْيَن).

642
00:50:28,996 --> 00:50:32,052
Musa(موسى) is continuing out, he's just marching out of Egypt.

643
00:50:32,202 --> 00:50:34,042
He reached to this area called Madyan(مَدْيَن);

644
00:50:34,128 --> 00:50:38,581
And there were some wells in that area; Abar(ابر); There's some water.

645
00:50:38,968 --> 00:50:47,912
There were men picking up water, drinking for themselves, feeding their goats and their camels.

646
00:50:48,956 --> 00:50:58,432
But then there were two women on the side, who had their sheep with them and they cannot drink any water.

647
00:50:59,832 --> 00:51:05,239
Keep in mind that Musa(موسى) is exhausted; tired from a long trip.

648
00:51:05,692 --> 00:51:13,663
The skin of his feet is peeled out; It is not time to intervene and help anyone.

649
00:51:14,236 --> 00:51:18,605
But because the personality of Musa(موسى) would not let any mistake pass by.

650
00:51:18,812 --> 00:51:22,998
He wanted to see why these two women are not drinking?

651
00:51:24,292 --> 00:51:28,853
So he walked up to them; And he said; What is the matter with you?

652
00:51:29,633 --> 00:51:32,254
They said; We cannot drink until these men leave.

653
00:51:32,320 --> 00:51:38,840
Because these men are pushing each other and fighting next to the water and everyone is getting water out by the strength of his muscle.

654
00:51:39,200 --> 00:51:42,252
How can these two women go and fight with them?

655
00:51:43,205 --> 00:51:47,732
Now Musa(موسى); who's exhausted and tired; can barely walk.

656
00:51:48,318 --> 00:51:51,681
He went in and he fought with these men

657
00:51:51,827 --> 00:51:55,789
and he pushed them aside and he brought out a few buckets of water.

658
00:51:55,935 --> 00:51:59,395
He provided it for the two women and for their sheep.

659
00:52:00,349 --> 00:52:06,956
And then Musa(موسى) could not handle it any further, he went and he laid down under a tree; completely exhausted.

660
00:52:08,070 --> 00:52:10,030
So he went down under a tree.

661
00:52:10,661 --> 00:52:11,361
And he said;

662
00:52:11,787 --> 00:52:18,887
رَبِّ إِنِّي لِمَا أَنزَلْتَ إِلَيَّ مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَقِيرٌ۝

663
00:52:19,863 --> 00:52:25,959
He said; Oh Allah, I am in need of any good that you can send down on me.

664
00:52:26,553 --> 00:52:29,114
Musa(موسى) was broke, he had nothing.

665
00:52:30,048 --> 00:52:37,608
So, he's telling Allahسُبحانه وتعالى anything, anything that you can give me, I need it, in this moment.

666
00:52:37,708 --> 00:52:40,418
إِنِّي لِمَا أَنزَلْتَ إِلَيَّ مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَقِير۝

667
00:52:40,448 --> 00:52:44,668
Oh Allah, whatever you're going to bestow on me; I need it.

668
00:52:47,014 --> 00:52:56,809
Musa(موسى) is making this Dua(دُعَا) and before the Dua(دُعَا) is over, the help of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى was already on its way.

669
00:52:57,975 --> 00:53:04,539
The Dua(دُعَا) has not done yet; And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is already sending the help to the direction of Musa(موسى).

670
00:53:07,192 --> 00:53:09,878
Who came and met Musa(موسى) under the tree?

671
00:53:10,325 --> 00:53:13,258
It was one of the women whom he supported.

672
00:53:14,245 --> 00:53:15,731
She came to Musa(موسى) and said;

673
00:53:16,225 --> 00:53:22,813
فَجَاءَتْهُ إِحْدَاهُمَا تَمْشِي عَلَى اسْتِحْيَاءٍ

674
00:53:22,993 --> 00:53:29,670
قَالَتْ إِنَّ أَبِي يَدْعُوكَ لِيَجْزِيَكَ أَجْرَ مَا سَقَيْتَ لَنَا ۚ

675
00:53:29,769 --> 00:53:33,697
Then there came to him one of the two women walking shyly.

676
00:53:34,090 --> 00:53:41,390
She said; verily my father calls you that, he may reward you for having watered for us.

677
00:53:42,117 --> 00:53:43,756
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

678
00:53:44,482 --> 00:53:46,062
عَلَى اسْتِحْيَاءٍ

679
00:53:46,932 --> 00:53:51,113
She was walking with Hayah(حياء); She had shyness.

680
00:53:52,087 --> 00:53:59,993
Shyness; Hayah(حياء) is a quality that men and women, in the West have lost.

681
00:54:01,540 --> 00:54:04,416
By the way Hayah(حياء) is not only for women; It's for men and women.

682
00:54:04,523 --> 00:54:12,870
We know that Sayidina Uthman Ibn Affanرضى الله عنه, was described as a man who has a lot of Hayah(حياء).

683
00:54:13,490 --> 00:54:20,798
And Rasool Allah ﷺ would sit in a certain way and represent himself to Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) in a certain way

684
00:54:20,964 --> 00:54:24,556
and when he was asked, Why don't you do that with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر).?

685
00:54:24,749 --> 00:54:29,749
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Shouldn't I be shy from a man who the angels are shy from?

686
00:54:30,316 --> 00:54:35,439
So this is not the quality only for women; It's also for men Hayah(حياء); shyness is a branch of Eeman(ايمان).

687
00:54:35,499 --> 00:54:36,712
شعبه من شعب الايمان

688
00:54:37,332 --> 00:54:42,701
This woman came to Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى) walking very shy.

689
00:54:43,101 --> 00:54:45,934
Shy, because she's dealing with an alien or foreign man.

690
00:54:45,994 --> 00:54:47,988
She doesn't know him; She was shy.

691
00:54:49,467 --> 00:54:51,227
The Muslim sister, she came.

692
00:54:51,257 --> 00:54:52,467
تَمْشِي عَلَى اسْتِحْيَاءٍ

693
00:54:52,567 --> 00:54:54,601
Walking with shyness.

694
00:54:55,827 --> 00:54:59,785
She said; My father wants to pay you; reward you, for what you have done.

695
00:55:00,498 --> 00:55:02,585
So, Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى) followed her.

696
00:55:02,865 --> 00:55:07,938
Some of the Salaf(سلف) say that, Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى) walked in front of her.

697
00:55:08,531 --> 00:55:12,513
Anyway, they reached there to meet this old man.

698
00:55:13,180 --> 00:55:15,320
He's old because the woman said;

699
00:55:15,350 --> 00:55:16,938
وَأَبُونَا شَيْخٌ كَبِيرٌ۝

700
00:55:17,253 --> 00:55:21,018
In the Ayah(آية) it says; our father is old; He's an old man.

701
00:55:21,284 --> 00:55:23,118
So Musa(موسى) went to visit this old man.

702
00:55:23,477 --> 00:55:30,363
Some of the Mufassireen(مفسرين) and actually many of the Mufassireen(مفسرين) say that, this man was Syedina Shoaibعليه الصلواة والسلام.

703
00:55:30,509 --> 00:55:33,356
 There is no evidence to support that from Qur'an or from Sunnah(سنة).

704
00:55:33,616 --> 00:55:38,364
But there is a strong opinion among many of the scholars of Tafseer(تفسير) of the Salaf(سلف).

705
00:55:38,545 --> 00:55:40,732
They say that, he was Syedina Shoaib(سيدنا شُعَيب).

706
00:55:41,352 --> 00:55:44,267
So Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى) went and met with him.

707
00:55:44,774 --> 00:55:46,374
فَلَمَّا قَصَّ عَلَيْهِ الْقَصَصَ

708
00:55:46,572 --> 00:55:49,894
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; So Musa(موسى) started narrating his story;

709
00:55:50,180 --> 00:55:53,031
Telling him the story of his life; It's a very interesting story.

710
00:55:53,271 --> 00:55:58,185
And Musa(موسى) started narrating that story to this old man.

711
00:55:58,438 --> 00:56:08,647
فَلَمَّا جَاءَهُ وَقَصَّ عَلَيْهِ الْقَصَصَ قَالَ لَا تَخَفْ ۖ نَجَوْتَ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الظَّالِمِينَ۝

712
00:56:08,742 --> 00:56:13,756
When Musa(موسى) mentioned his story to the old man, the old man told him;

713
00:56:13,836 --> 00:56:18,328
Do not fear; You are now safe from the oppressor people.

714
00:56:18,555 --> 00:56:21,387
He's telling him; you have crossed the border; You're out of Egypt now.

715
00:56:21,528 --> 00:56:23,851
So don't worry, it's safe for you over here;

716
00:56:24,104 --> 00:56:25,024
He was in Madyan(مَدْيَن).

717
00:56:25,231 --> 00:56:29,102
Syedina Musaعليه السلام when he left from Egypt.

718
00:56:29,955 --> 00:56:32,904
He didn't know where he's going; He never traveled out of Egypt.

719
00:56:32,934 --> 00:56:36,752
He just walked toward the east trying to get out of Egypt.

720
00:56:37,112 --> 00:56:42,446
And now this man is telling him; you have crossed the border and now you have reached to safety.

721
00:56:42,686 --> 00:56:49,177
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; You have escaped from the people who are Dhualimeen(ظالمين); the oppressors.

722
00:56:50,084 --> 00:56:54,871
This daughter; she went to her father and she gave him a wonderful advice.

723
00:56:55,064 --> 00:56:56,938
She told him; Oh my father! hire him.

724
00:56:57,184 --> 00:57:02,004
قَالَتْ إِحْدَاهُمَا يَا أَبَتِ اسْتَأْجِرْهُ ۖ

725
00:57:02,104 --> 00:57:05,244
And one of them said; Oh my father! hire him.

726
00:57:06,497 --> 00:57:09,044
And she gave the reasons; why you should hire him.

727
00:57:10,097 --> 00:57:11,284
What did she say?

728
00:57:11,604 --> 00:57:14,590
They said that this woman was very wise; What did she say?

729
00:57:14,690 --> 00:57:19,413
إِنَّ خَيْرَ مَنِ اسْتَأْجَرْتَ الْقَوِيُّ الْأَمِينُ۝

730
00:57:19,671 --> 00:57:23,437
The best man to hire is the strong and the trustworthy.

731
00:57:23,770 --> 00:57:28,479
These are two qualities you want to search for; in the employer.

732
00:57:29,306 --> 00:57:31,733
Strength and trustworthiness.

733
00:57:32,339 --> 00:57:35,493
What does strength mean? Quwwah(قوة); Qawi(قوى); he's strong.

734
00:57:36,113 --> 00:57:39,718
This is relevant to the kind of job that will be done.

735
00:57:40,485 --> 00:57:45,626
If it is a physically demanding job, then the strength means strong in his physical body.

736
00:57:45,920 --> 00:57:50,740
If it's an intellectual kind of job, then you need to be strong in your mind.

737
00:57:51,273 --> 00:57:54,665
To summarize it; you need to be very strong in your field.

738
00:57:55,778 --> 00:57:58,311
That is what is meant by Qawi(قوى); strong.

739
00:57:58,791 --> 00:58:00,267
Al-Amin(الامين); Trustworthy.

740
00:58:00,297 --> 00:58:01,587
It's not enough to be strong.

741
00:58:02,041 --> 00:58:06,499
Because you could be strong but you're using your strengths against your organization.

742
00:58:07,299 --> 00:58:10,412
You could be using it for your own benefit and harming the others.

743
00:58:10,645 --> 00:58:12,605
So you have to be trustworthy too.

744
00:58:13,645 --> 00:58:19,971
And that's why Abu Bakrرضى الله عنه, when he appointed Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) to be the Khalifah(خليفه);

745
00:58:20,178 --> 00:58:22,113
he told the Muslims, why he appointed him?

746
00:58:22,340 --> 00:58:25,273
He said; The best man to appoint on you is Al-Qawwi(القوى), Al-Amin(الامين);

747
00:58:25,667 --> 00:58:27,088
The strong and The trustworthy.

748
00:58:27,375 --> 00:58:29,188
They learn their rules from Qur'an.

749
00:58:29,568 --> 00:58:36,418
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) did not go through any political science classes or degrees.

750
00:58:36,838 --> 00:58:40,312
He learned the politics of Islam from Qur'an.

751
00:58:41,512 --> 00:58:45,933
So when he wanted to hire somebody or to appoint somebody to the position of Khilafah(خِلَافَه);

752
00:58:46,400 --> 00:58:52,796
He has a whole generation of Sahaba(صحابه) in front of his eyes; All of them are righteous.

753
00:58:53,123 --> 00:58:55,483
Righteousness is common among all of the Sahabah(صحابه).

754
00:58:55,742 --> 00:58:57,691
So, how can you choose among them?

755
00:58:57,871 --> 00:59:02,597
He looked for these two qualities: Quwwah(قوة) and Amanah(امانه); Strength and Trustworthiness.

756
00:59:03,971 --> 00:59:09,991
So, the father offered the job to Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى),

757
00:59:10,871 --> 00:59:13,713
but he went a little further; he took another step.

758
00:59:14,219 --> 00:59:17,279
He also offered Musa(موسى) one of his daughters.

759
00:59:18,686 --> 00:59:20,110
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

760
00:59:20,330 --> 00:59:27,049
قَالَ إِنِّىٓ أُرِيدُ أَنْ أُنكِحَكَ إِحْدَى ٱبْنَتَىَّ هَٰتَيْنِ عَلَىٰٓ

761
00:59:27,349 --> 00:59:31,789
عَلَىٰٓ أَن تَأْجُرَنِى ثَمَٰنِىَ حِجَجٍۢ ۖ

762
00:59:31,962 --> 00:59:36,066
فَإِنْ أَتْمَمْتَ عَشْرًا فَمِنْ عِندِكَ ۖ

763
00:59:36,346 --> 00:59:40,433
وَمَآ أُرِيدُ أَنْ أَشُقَّ عَلَيْكَ ۚ

764
00:59:40,653 --> 00:59:47,117
سَتَجِدُنِىٓ إِن شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ۝

765
00:59:47,195 --> 00:59:56,050
He said; I intend to wed you one of these two daughters of mine; on condition that you serve me for eight years,

766
00:59:56,280 --> 00:59:59,773
but if you complete 10; it would be a favor from you.

767
00:59:59,986 --> 01:00:05,936
But I intend not to place you under a difficulty; If Allah will; you will find me one of the righteous.

768
01:00:06,576 --> 01:00:11,176
So, he said; I will marry you one of my daughters; what is the Maher(مهر) that you will pay me?

769
01:00:11,702 --> 01:00:13,546
You work for me for eight years.

770
01:00:14,233 --> 01:00:21,100
And if you want to complete 10 years, that's up to you; It's not part of our agreement.

771
01:00:21,333 --> 01:00:25,973
But I would suggest it; if you want to work for 10 years, that will be better.

772
01:00:26,719 --> 01:00:29,399
But the bottom line is you have to work for minimum of eight.

773
01:00:29,653 --> 01:00:32,167
Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى) to make it clear, he said;

774
01:00:32,374 --> 01:00:35,434
قَالَ ذَٰلِكَ بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَكَ ۖ

775
01:00:35,627 --> 01:00:45,571
أَيَّمَا الْأَجَلَيْنِ قَضَيْتُ فَلَا عُدْوَانَ عَلَيَّ ۖ وَاللَّهُ عَلَىٰ مَا نَقُولُ وَكِيلٌ۝

776
01:00:45,658 --> 01:00:47,783
Musa(موسى) wanted to be clear about this agreement.

777
01:00:47,830 --> 01:00:51,470
He said, that is a settled deal between me and you,

778
01:00:51,500 --> 01:01:00,447
whichever of the two terms I fulfill, there will be no injustice to me, and Allah is surety over what we say.

779
01:01:00,772 --> 01:01:06,303
Musa(موسى) is saying; If I work for eight years; Don't blame me; Don't commit any injustice to me.

780
01:01:06,723 --> 01:01:09,136
The agreement is that, I work for eight years with you.

781
01:01:10,696 --> 01:01:18,090
Rasool Allah ﷺ asked Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل); which of the two terms that Musa(موسى) fulfill?

782
01:01:18,350 --> 01:01:20,795
Did he work for eight or did he work for ten?

783
01:01:21,192 --> 01:01:25,572
Jibreelعليه السلام  told Muhammadﷺ ;

784
01:01:26,019 --> 01:01:27,519
اتمها واكملها

785
01:01:27,623 --> 01:01:30,981
That he worked for the best and the most complete, and that is ten years.

786
01:01:31,807 --> 01:01:39,023
This is the Ihsaan(احسان) and Itqan(اتقان) perfection of your work, even though the agreement was clear that, I have to work for eight years.

787
01:01:39,240 --> 01:01:42,116
But he completed it and he worked for ten.

788
01:01:43,156 --> 01:01:47,369
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تسليما كثيرا

